  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nAnomalous upper level ridging extends eastward into the Great Lakes \nand Ohio Valley this week while high pressure at the surface remains \nover the region. Hot and rain free conditions, with highs in the \nlower 90s are likely through at least Thursday. Peak afternoon heat \nindex values reach into the upper 90s to near 100 when factoring in \ndew points in the upper 60s. The hottest day of the week will likely \nbe Wednesday. Borderline Heat Advisory conditions are expected the \nmiddle of this week with dew points being the main limiting factor.  \n\nThe upper level ridge starts to break the end of this week when a \nlow pressure system is forecast to move through the Great Lakes. \nShower and storm chances increase with this low moving into the \nregion this weekend and temperatures cool slightly.",
